# Client UI

## Mods and types

- Project tabs are `mods` tuples: `[type, name, data]`.
- `mod[0]` is the tab type: `Board` | `Notes` | `Files` | `Database` | …
- `TYPES` in `utils.js` with `off: true` are roadmap stubs — don’t delete casually; don’t build full UI unless asked.

## Where logic lives

- Components own UI and local interaction state.
- Shared pure logic → `utils.js` / `db*.js` / `flipSwap.js`.
- All HTTP → `src/api.js` only (use existing `apiJson` helpers).

## Reuse these primitives

- Menus / selects: `Dropdown.jsx`
- Icons: `Icon` / `IC` from `icons.jsx`
- Confirm / prompt: `askConfirm` / `askPrompt`
- Neighbor FLIP reorder: `flipSwapHorizontal` from `flipSwap.js`
- Timelog card identity: `taskKey` / `timelogTaskFromCard` from `utils.js`

## Menus

When adding a “⋮ more” menu, copy an existing more-menu (TabBar / Board / Timelogs / Files) or extract a shared shell — do not invent a new popover pattern.

## Styles

- Put styles in `src/index.css`. Match existing class naming; no new CSS framework or CSS modules unless asked.
